## Chalk (calcium carbonate)
component-calcium-carbonate = Chalk (calcium carbonate)
    .genitive = chalk
component-calcium-carbonate-description-novice = Chalk, marble, limestone, eggshells and seashells are made of it. It barely dissolves in water, but in vinegar it fizzes and slowly disappears.
component-calcium-carbonate-description-school = Calcium carbonate reacts with acids, releasing carbon dioxide. Strongly heated, it breaks down into quicklime (CaO) and CO₂.
component-calcium-carbonate-model-notes = The decomposition temperature is not checked against sources yet, so chalk does not decompose in the model.
